WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back. We're here with
Colin Jost and Michael Che.

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:04.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jost, you guys both
made some sketch appearances,

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:06.239 size:84% position:42%
which doesn't happen
that often on the show.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.241
You were in
a Kool-Aid commercial, which --

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
There you go.
-Yes.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
Michael Che cast me
in his Kool-Aid commercial.

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:12.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-We're basically only

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
put in sketches --
at least me --

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:16.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they say,
"We have no cast available."

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-The shoot's at 5:00 a.m.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.053 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Only Jost will come.

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're cheaper
than hiring an extra?

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
I'm just like an extra.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.493
-Che, you have done some
cast work on the show, as well.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:30.497
There you are.
You're the Scarecrow right here.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:31.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:34.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In a version of "The Wiz"
with, of course, Ryan Gosling.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.301 line:92%
Who else would be in "The Wiz"?

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:39.272
But it was -- the best burn on
Che is that he's a Scarecrow.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.841
You cannot tell it's him,
and he spent like six hours

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
in makeup all the time
to get into it.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The best is everyone
calls me "Black Scarecrow,"

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm like,
"It's just Scarecrow."

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:51.251 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:53.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were
in a Scientology ad, Jost?

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:56.589
-I was -- Scientol -- yes.
-You're very believable.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.458
-I know.
That's really one of my finest.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You played
Lester Holt on the show.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Which was wonderful,

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.464 line:92%
but then there was an article.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:06.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
The title of the article is
"Watching History:

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
Find out all
the familiar TV faces

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.170 size:81% position:41%
covering the final lap
of the 2016 election."

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so this was
an actual newspaper article,

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.407 line:92%
or online newspaper article.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:17.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anderson Cooper, Megyn Kelly,
and then you.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.813 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:22.449
-Yeah.
-Your Lester Holt was so good...

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, shout-out
to the makeup department.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.853 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:30.256
-But this is very -- you did --
This was a bit you did

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "Update"
where you played Gretchen.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:35.428
-You went undercover
as a white girl named Gretchen.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
I went undercover as a liberal
white woman named Gretchen,

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:42.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I didn't use makeup,
but it was still believable.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:43.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:47.373
-And then you guys had an idea,
like a second round of this.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Now, so the idea --

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
Explain how
it was supposed to work.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The last show,
we had an idea that got cut --

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.117
that was -- I said to Che,
"Well, you went undercover

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.518 line:92%
as a white woman named Gretchen

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
to try to figure out
that situation."

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.789
And I had been reading all this
terrible stuff about R. Kelly,

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I thought
maybe I could go undercover

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:09.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a black teenage girl
to try to entrap R. Kelly.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.631 line:92%
[ Laughter, audience groans ]

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes, exactly, boos.
Thank you.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's, uh --
You know what?

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
That sounds like
a man of Manny Manimals.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:20.673 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:24.644
-Well, the idea was, I knew
it was the worst idea ever.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
So you did not shoot it.

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:28.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, the idea
was Che would stop me

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
and point out
how awful of an idea that was,

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:33.786
and I would say, "Really?
It doesn't go both ways?"

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:34.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was like,
"Absolutely not."

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Oh, yeah, that makes sense."

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-And then it said,
"The more you know."

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like the little --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:41.227 size:84% position:42%
♪♪ "The more you --" ♪♪
Yeah, you could tell.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.296 size:88% position:44%
We're glad it was cut.
I think that seems fair.

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
The audience approves.
-I begged him not to do it.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:46.332 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:50.170
-How often -- one of my favorite
things you guys do,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you did
for the Christmas show, right?

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where you make each other
read jokes

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the other one
has not seen first.

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-You seem to have a lot of fun

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:59.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
putting each other
in uncomfortable situations.

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:01.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-He made --

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
The slug came up for one
he made me tell,

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.052
which was
National Rosa Parks Day came up,

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the joke he made me tell
without having read it,

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:11.191
and my family said they were all
-- like, lost their breath.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:12.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And they were like,

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We're watching
our son's end right now."

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Do you remember the joke?

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:19.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I don't.
-That's for the best.

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:22.635 size:84% position:42%
James McAvoy this week.
He should be fantastic.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:23.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God, yeah.
He's great.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
He already plays 12 different
characters in "Split."

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. That's basically
a whole episode.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
We're good.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll just do each of those.
He's great.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was on your show.
-He's incredibly charming,

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:34.647
great actor, so I'm really
looking forward to that.

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.883
Gentlemen, it's always so great
to have you here.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:37.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
Warm up.
We got you a space heater

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
back in your dressing room.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:42.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
Colin Jost and Michael Che,
everybody.

